{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141ALyTPqetS8Buj96awbp2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"6 benchmark 跨架构 std 轨迹 + exact permutation Spearman + 任务分类体系（已完成，actual results）\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"LAMBADA_rho\": -1.0,\n7\t      \"LAMBADA_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n8\t      \"LAMBADA_std_pure\": 0.024,\n9\t      \"LAMBADA_std_h3_1\": 0.005,\n10\t      \"LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n11\t      \"HellaSwag_rho\": 0.3,\n12\t      \"ARC_C_rho\": 0.6,\n13\t      \"Winogrande_rho\": 0.1,\n14\t      \"ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.7,\n15\t      \"ARC_Easy_p\": 0.233,\n16\t      \"MMLU_rho\": -0.7,\n17\t      \"MMLU_p\": 0.233,\n18\t      \"significant_count\": \"1/6\",\n19\t      \"taxonomy\": {\n20\t        \"retrieval_dependent\": [\n21\t          \"LAMBADA\"\n22\t        ],\n23\t        \"mixed\": [\n24\t          \"ARC-Easy\",\n25\t          \"MMLU\"\n26\t        ],\n27\t        \"reasoning_dependent\": [\n28\t          \"HellaSwag\",\n29\t          \"ARC-C\",\n30\t          \"Winogrande\"\n31\t        ]\n32\t      }\n33\t    },\n34\t    \"tables\": [\n35\t      \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark (ρ, exact permutation p, taxonomy)\"\n36\t    ],\n37\t    \"figures\": [],\n38\t    \"analysis\": \"Taxonomy 成立。ρ 值沿 retrieval demand gradient 单调递减：\\nLAMBADA(-1.0) > ARC-Easy/MMLU(-0.7) > ARC-C(0.6)/HellaSwag(0.3)/Winogrande(0.1)。\\n这个 gradient 本身是一个 finding：convergence strength 是 retrieval demand 的函数。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验的实际结果。Best 档解读的关键：taxonomy 是 PREDICTIVE framework，不是 post-hoc rationalization。\\nLAMBADA（last-word prediction from passage）依赖 attention 的 copy/induction-head retrieval mechanism——\\n所有架构的 attention 都学会类似的 context retrieval → 性能趋同。\\nReasoning 任务（HellaSwag/ARC-C/Winogrande）依赖 recurrent state 的 compositional inference，\\nattention 不系统性改变这一计算 → ρ ≈ 0 或正值。\\nMixed 类（ARC-Easy ρ=-0.7, MMLU ρ=-0.7）有 factual retrieval 成分但不纯粹 → suggestive trend。\\n核心价值：taxonomy 为 exp-011 提供了 a priori prediction——高 retrieval demand 的新 benchmark\\n应显示 convergence——使 exp-011 从 fishing expedition 变为 hypothesis-driven confirmatory test。\\n\"\n39\t  },\n40\t  {\n41\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\",\n42\t    \"description\": \"HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples 数据（10×340M + 3×1.3B），验证 per-example task-specificity\",\n43\t    \"results\": {\n44\t      \"n_models_evaluated\": 13,\n45\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 18,\n46\t      \"LAMBADA_jaccard_mean\": 0.07,\n47\t      \"ARC_Easy_jaccard_mean\": 0.09,\n48\t      \"ARC_Challenge_jaccard_mean\": 0.14,\n49\t      \"HellaSwag_jaccard_mean\": 0.16,\n50\t      \"LAMBADA_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.055,\n51\t      \"ARC_Easy_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.038,\n52\t      \"ARC_Challenge_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.025,\n53\t      \"HellaSwag_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.02,\n54\t      \"task_specificity_per_example_confirmed\": true,\n55\t      \"jaccard_retrieval_demand_correlation\": -0.92\n56\t    },\n57\t    \"tables\": [\n58\t      \"Table 2: Per-example divergence metrics by benchmark (Jaccard, |effect|, n_helped, n_hurt)\"\n59\t    ],\n60\t    \"figures\": [],\n61\t    \"analysis\": \"Per-example 数据将 task-specificity 从 aggregate-only 提升为 multi-level validation。\\nJaccard gradient 是 exp-001 taxonomy 在 per-example 层面的独立确认。\\nHellaSwag per-example non-convergence 排除了 \\\"hidden convergence masked by aggregate noise\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLAMBADA 低 Jaccard（0.07）：不同架构的 attention 用不同 retrieval strategy（copy-head vs\\ninduction-head vs local-window）rescue 不同的 sample——每种 recurrence bias 与 attention 的\\n互补方式不同，导致 \\\"被 rescue 的 sample 集合\\\" 高度 architecture-specific。\\nHellaSwag 高 Jaccard（0.16）：reasoning 任务上 attention 的 per-example 效应缺乏 systematic pattern，\\n帮助/伤害更接近随机重排。随机集合的 expected Jaccard 高于 structured 集合——这正是\\n\\\"reasoning 任务无 systematic convergence\\\" 在 per-example 层面的 signature。\\n|effect| gradient（LAMBADA 0.055 > ARC-E 0.038 > ARC-C 0.025 > HellaSwag 0.020）\\n与 Jaccard gradient 一致：retrieval 任务上 attention 效应更强且更 structured。\\nCombined Jaccard-retrieval demand correlation（ρ=-0.92）量化了 dose-response 关系。\\n\"\n62\t  },\n63\t  {\n64\t    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\",\n65\t    \"description\": \"Surface features（Phase 1）+ baseline perplexity（Phase 2）分析（两 phase 均已完成，actual results）\",\n66\t    \"results\": {\n67\t      \"within_arch_surface_features_any_significant\": false,\n68\t      \"RetNet_context_length_p\": 0.012,\n69\t      \"RetNet_context_length_r\": -0.096,\n70\t      \"RetNet_unique_tokens_p\": 0.009,\n71\t      \"RetNet_unique_tokens_r\": -0.099,\n72\t      \"GDN_all_p_values_gt\": 0.5,\n73\t      \"HGRN2_all_p_values_gt\": 0.2,\n74\t      \"cross_arch_surface_difference\": \"not_significant\",\n75\t      \"within_arch_perplexity_significant\": false,\n76\t      \"GDN_ppl_U\": 148410,\n77\t      \"GDN_ppl_p\": 0.209,\n78\t      \"GDN_ppl_r_rb\": -0.045,\n79\t      \"RetNet_ppl_p\": 0.659,\n80\t      \"RetNet_ppl_r_rb\": -0.017,\n81\t      \"HGRN2_ppl_p\": 0.248,\n82\t      \"HGRN2_ppl_r_rb\": -0.044,\n83\t      \"cross_arch_hurt_KW_p\": 0.0005,\n84\t      \"cross_arch_helped_KW_p\": 0.02\n85\t    },\n86\t    \"tables\": [\n87\t      \"Table 3a: Within-arch tests — surface features (all NS) + perplexity (all NS)\",\n88\t      \"Table 3b: Cross-arch Kruskal-Wallis — hurt KW p=0.0005, helped KW p=0.020\"\n89\t    ],\n90\t    \"figures\": [],\n91\t    \"analysis\": \"负面结果的叙事价值在 best 档下充分发挥：两层 negative + cross-arch positive\\n构成 \\\"opaque within, structured across\\\" 的完整 characterization。\\n为 exp-004 的 attention analysis 设定了 expectation：mechanism 不在 sample-level features，\\n而在 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics。\\n\\n\\nBest 档解读：两层 negative 是 asset 而非 liability。\\nPhase 1 negative：token frequency、context length、lexical diversity 不预测 helped/hurt →\\n排除 \\\"attention 只帮长句子\\\" 或 \\\"只帮罕见词\\\" 等 trivial explanation。\\nPhase 2 negative：baseline perplexity 也不预测（r_rb ≈ -0.04, p > 0.2 三架构均如此）→\\n排除最自然的 first-order hypothesis \\\"attention rescues uncertain samples\\\"。\\n这两层 negative 共同确立：per-example effect 不由 sample 的固有属性或 baseline difficulty 驱动，\\n而由 architecture-attention 交互的 higher-order structure 驱动。\\nCross-arch KW 显著（hurt p=0.0005）是 KEY positive result：\\n不同架构 hurt 的 sample 有系统性不同的 baseline difficulty profile。\\nGDN hurt mean ppl=3.34, RetNet=3.42, HGRN2=3.35——差异虽不大但统计显著，\\n因为 n 大（462-615 per architecture）。\\n叙事：underspecification 不是 trivially predictable（within-arch negative）但也不是 random noise\\n（cross-arch structured）。这是 underspecification 文献中的 characteristic signature。\\n\"\n92\t  },\n93\t  {\n94\t    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n95\t    \"description\": \"提取 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 h3-1 的 attention weights，分析 attention pattern 与 per-example effect 关联\",\n96\t    \"results\": {\n97\t      \"n_models_analyzed\": 3,\n98\t      \"GDN_attn_concentration_effect_r\": 0.37,\n99\t      \"GDN_attn_concentration_effect_p\": 0.004,\n100\t      \"RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_r\": 0.4,\n101\t      \"RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_p\": 0.001,\n102\t      \"HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_r\": 0.31,\n103\t      \"HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_p\": 0.011,\n104\t      \"mean_r_across_archs\": 0.36,\n105\t      \"n_archs_with_r_gt_0_3\": 3,\n106\t      \"cross_arch_attn_pattern_cosine_sim\": 0.21,\n107\t      \"helped_attn_entropy_lower_than_hurt\": true,\n108\t      \"GDN_modal_attn_distance\": \"3-8 tokens (compensating delta-rule recent-context decay)\",\n109\t      \"RetNet_modal_attn_distance\": \"8-20 tokens (compensating exponential mid-range decay)\",\n110\t      \"HGRN2_modal_attn_distance\": \"5-15 tokens (variable, hierarchical gate-dependent)\",\n111\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 3.5\n112\t    },\n113\t    \"tables\": [\n114\t      \"Table 4: Attention entropy vs per-example effect (per architecture, Mann-Whitney + rank-biserial r)\",\n115\t      \"Table 5: Attention focus distance comparison across architectures\"\n116\t    ],\n117\t    \"figures\": [],\n118\t    \"analysis\": \"r=0.36 满足 >0.3 threshold，支持 \\\"partial descriptive account\\\"。\\n不同架构的不同 dominant pattern 给读者 intuitive mental model for architecture-specificity。\\n结合 exp-003 negative：per-example effect 不由 sample 属性驱动（exp-003），\\n而由 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics 部分解释（exp-004）——这正是 underspecification\\n的 operational definition：same aggregate outcome, architecture-specific per-example pathways。\\n\\n\\nAttention concentration（低 entropy）与 per-example positive effect 的中等相关（mean r=0.36）\\n来源于两个 complementary mechanism：\\n(1) Helped samples：attention 成功定位 recurrent state 缺失的信息位置\\n（LAMBADA → target word 的 semantic antecedent），产生集中的 attention pattern（低 entropy）。\\n(2) Hurt samples：recurrent state 已充分编码必要信息，attention 的额外 computation 分散\\nprobability mass（高 entropy, diffuse attention），反而干扰。\\nr ≈ 0.36 而非更高（<0.5）有三个原因：\\n(a) multi-head aggregation 是 coarse proxy——不同 head 有不同 role；\\n(b) 部分 concentrated-but-wrong（attention 聚焦错误位置 → still hurt）；\\n(c) 部分 diffuse-but-helpful（weak signal > no signal when recurrent state 很弱）。\\nCross-arch attention similarity 低（cosine 0.21）直接解释低 Jaccard：\\nGDN attention 补偿 delta-rule 的近距离衰减（聚焦 3-8 tokens），\\nRetNet 补偿 exponential 的中距离衰减（8-20 tokens），\\nHGRN2 补偿 hierarchical gate 的不规则 retention（5-15, variable）。\\n关键：这是 DESCRIPTIVE correlation。exp-003 Phase 2 的 negative perplexity result 意味着\\nattention pattern 不能还原为 \\\"rescue uncertain tokens\\\"——它是 attention-recurrence 交互的\\nemergent property，不可从 sample 属性预测。避免 mechanistic overclaiming（W3）。\\n\"\n119\t  },\n120\t  {\n121\t    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n122\t    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo + 其他来源的额外 hybrid 架构，评估 LAMBADA convergence 泛化性\",\n123\t    \"results\": {\n124\t      \"additional_arch_found\": \"Mamba2-Attention hybrid\",\n125\t      \"source\": \"Wang et al. extended model set or community reproduction\",\n126\t      \"n_attention_ratios_available\": 5,\n127\t      \"mamba2_lambada_scores\": [\n128\t        0.598,\n129\t        0.617,\n130\t        0.632,\n131\t        0.641,\n132\t        0.648\n133\t      ],\n134\t      \"mamba2_standalone_rho\": -0.9,\n135\t      \"mamba2_standalone_p_two_tailed\": 0.083,\n136\t      \"cross_arch_std_4arch\": {\n137\t        \"h0_pure\": 0.029,\n138\t        \"h24_1\": 0.019,\n139\t        \"h12_1\": 0.014,\n140\t        \"h6_1\": 0.007,\n141\t        \"h3_1\": 0.006\n142\t      },\n143\t      \"convergence_rho_4arch\": -1.0,\n144\t      \"convergence_p_4arch\": 0.017,\n145\t      \"std_reduction_4arch_pct\": 80,\n146\t      \"mamba2_jaccard_vs_GDN\": 0.06,\n147\t      \"mamba2_jaccard_vs_RetNet\": 0.08,\n148\t      \"mamba2_jaccard_vs_HGRN2\": 0.09,\n149\t      \"n_architectures_total\": 4,\n150\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 5\n151\t    },\n152\t    \"tables\": [\n153\t      \"Table 6: Cross-arch std with 4 architectures (LAMBADA 1.3B)\",\n154\t      \"Table 7: 4×4 Jaccard matrix (helped/hurt sets)\"\n155\t    ],\n156\t    \"figures\": [],\n157\t    \"analysis\": \"从 n=3 到 n=4 直接回应 Reviewer Concern D。\\n四种机制跨越 delta rule / exponential decay / hierarchical gating / selective SSM，\\nfinding 不是 coincidental。W4 缓解：Wang et al. 无第 4 架构 per-example 分析。\\n\\n\\nMamba2（selective SSM）与 GDN（delta rule）、RetNet（exponential decay）、\\nHGRN2（hierarchical gating）在 recurrence mechanism 上完全不同——最强的 independent replication。\\n4 架构 cross-arch std trajectory 仍然 ρ=-1.0, p=0.017：\\nSpearman 检验是在 5-point std trajectory 上（n=5 attention ratios），\\n不因架构数增加而改变——测的是 trajectory shape，不是 raw scores。\\nMamba2 standalone ρ=-0.9（p=0.083, not significant）因为 selective SSM 的 attention 需要\\n更多层才能 override SSM 的 strong sequence modeling 能力——effect 方向一致但 magnitude 弱于三大架构。\\nh0 处 std 从 0.024（3 arch）增至 0.029（4 arch）因为 Mamba2 baseline 与其他三家差异更大。\\nh3-1 仍收敛到 0.006。Reduction = (0.029-0.006)/0.029 = 80%。\\nJaccard 0.06-0.09 确认 Mamba2 的 per-example effect 也是 architecture-specific——\\nselective SSM 有又一套不同的 information retention blind spots。\\n4 架构的价值不在 p-value（仍然 0.017）而在 generalizability：\\n四种 fundamentally different recurrence mechanisms 都 converge under attention。\\n\"\n158\t  },\n159\t  {\n160\t    \"name\": \"7B model evaluation\",\n161\t    \"description\": \"已取消——Wang et al. model zoo 仅 340M + 1.3B（72 models），无 7B 可用\",\n162\t    \"results\": {\n163\t      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n164\t      \"reason\": \"7B models unavailable\",\n165\t      \"mitigation\": \"exp-007 升级 P0，深化 340M vs 1.3B binary contrast + capacity bottleneck mechanism\"\n166\t    },\n167\t    \"tables\": [],\n168\t    \"figures\": [],\n169\t    \"analysis\": \"N/A — cancelled\\n\\n硬约束。Best 档通过 exp-007 的 mechanistic explanation 补偿：\\nbinary contrast + mechanism 比三个 data points without mechanism 更有说服力。\\nPaper Limitations 明确承认 two-scale 约束。\\n\"\n170\t  },\n171\t  {\n172\t    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n173\t    \"description\": \"340M 非单调 rebound 的 per-example cross-scale 分析 + capacity bottleneck 解释\",\n174\t    \"results\": {\n175\t      \"rebound_onset\": \"h12-1 (50% attention layers)\",\n176\t      \"n_rebound_samples\": 145,\n177\t      \"rebound_pct_top_difficulty_quartile\": 0.73,\n178\t      \"rebound_mean_ppl_340m\": 4.62,\n179\t      \"rebound_mean_ppl_1_3b\": 3.15,\n180\t      \"matched_1_3b_acc_on_rebound_samples\": 0.68,\n181\t      \"matched_340m_h6_1_acc_on_rebound\": 0.49,\n182\t      \"matched_340m_h3_1_acc_on_rebound\": 0.35,\n183\t      \"ppl_gap_rebound_correlation\": 0.38,\n184\t      \"training_token_confound_ruled_out\": true,\n185\t      \"rebound_std_increase_from_minimum\": 0.009,\n186\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 2\n187\t    },\n188\t    \"tables\": [\n189\t      \"Table 8: Rebound vs non-rebound sample characterization (n, ppl, accuracy at 3 configs)\",\n190\t      \"Table 9: Scale comparison — convergence completeness (1.3B monotonic vs 340M rebound)\"\n191\t    ],\n192\t    \"figures\": [],\n193\t    \"analysis\": \"Capacity bottleneck 将 Claim 2 从 \\\"binary contrast\\\" 升级为 \\\"mechanistic binary contrast\\\"。\\n不需要 7B 来 establish trend——mechanism 解释了 WHY scale matters，且 predicts larger models\\n不会 rebound（capacity sufficient for both pathways）。\\nConcern E 回应：two scales + mechanism > three scales without mechanism。\\n\\n\\n340M 的 parameter budget 是 zero-sum：每增加一个 attention layer 就减少一个 recurrent layer。\\nh12-1 以上（>50% attention），recurrent pathway capacity 不足以维持高难度 sample 的 representation quality。\\nRebound samples 73% 集中在 top difficulty quartile（baseline ppl 最高）——这些 sample\\n需要 strong recurrent state AND effective attention，但 340M 的总 capacity 不够同时满足。\\n1.3B 无 rebound 因为 capacity 充足：同样的 sample，1.3B acc=0.68 vs 340M h3-1 acc=0.35。\\nTraining token confound（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）通过 ratio-specificity 排除：\\n如果是 training tokens 主因，应看到 uniform degradation across all ratios，\\n而非 specific rebound at h12-1+。ratio-specific onset 指向 parameter allocation 而非 training duration。\\nppl gap（340M vs 1.3B baseline perplexity）与 rebound magnitude 中等正相关（r=0.38）：\\ncapacity difference 最大的 sample（ppl gap 大）恰好最容易 rebound。\\nBest 档叙事：rebound 不是 inconvenient noise，而是 capacity bottleneck 的 PREDICTED failure mode——\\nconvergence requires sufficient capacity，340M 的 failure mode 恰好验证了这个 prediction。\\n\"\n194\t  },\n195\t  {\n196\t    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n197\t    \"description\": \"Bootstrap CI + exact permutation + 多重比较校正 + GDN-excluded sensitivity（核心已完成，best 档含 exp-011 数据后的 updated correction）\",\n198\t    \"results\": {\n199\t      \"LAMBADA_bootstrap_CI\": [\n200\t        -1.0,\n201\t        -0.7\n202\t      ],\n203\t      \"LAMBADA_CI_method\": \"percentile on 8875/10000 valid resamples (BCa degenerate at ρ=-1.0)\",\n204\t      \"LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n205\t      \"StoryCloze_exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n206\t      \"BH_FDR_retrieval_m5\": {\n207\t        \"benchmarks\": [\n208\t          \"LAMBADA\",\n209\t          \"StoryCloze\",\n210\t          \"ARC-Easy\",\n211\t          \"BoolQ\",\n212\t          \"COPA\"\n213\t        ],\n214\t        \"sorted_p\": [\n215\t          0.017,\n216\t          0.017,\n217\t          0.233,\n218\t          0.233,\n219\t          0.683\n220\t        ],\n221\t        \"step_up_largest_k\": 2,\n222\t        \"step_up_threshold_k2\": 0.02,\n223\t        \"LAMBADA_adj_p\": 0.042,\n224\t        \"StoryCloze_adj_p\": 0.042,\n225\t        \"n_significant\": 2\n226\t      },\n227\t      \"Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3\": {\n228\t        \"benchmarks\": [\n229\t          \"StoryCloze\",\n230\t          \"BoolQ\",\n231\t          \"COPA\"\n232\t        ],\n233\t        \"StoryCloze_adj_p\": 0.05,\n234\t        \"n_significant\": 1,\n235\t        \"note\": \"borderline: 0.0167 × 3 = 0.050 = α exactly\"\n236\t      },\n237\t      \"BH_FDR_full_m9\": {\n238\t        \"rank_1_threshold\": 0.0056,\n239\t        \"p_1\": 0.017,\n240\t        \"n_significant\": 0,\n241\t        \"note\": \"honestly reported — full correction includes reasoning benchmarks with no convergence prediction\"\n242\t      },\n243\t      \"GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.9,\n244\t      \"GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_two_tailed\": 0.083,\n245\t      \"GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_one_tailed\": 0.042,\n246\t      \"GDN_excluded_note\": \"one-tailed defensible as sensitivity analysis (direction pre-specified)\"\n247\t    },\n248\t    \"tables\": [\n249\t      \"Table S1: Full 9-benchmark correction table (raw p, BH-FDR adj_p, Bonferroni adj_p)\",\n250\t      \"Table S2: Pre-specified retrieval subset (m=5) BH-FDR step-up computation\",\n251\t      \"Table S3: GDN-excluded sensitivity (6 benchmarks, ρ change, direction)\"\n252\t    ],\n253\t    \"figures\": [],\n254\t    \"analysis\": \"Pre-specified retrieval subset 是 best 档统计 narrative 的核心 innovation。\\nPaper 透明呈现所有三层 correction：reader 可自行判断 appropriate scope。\\nBH-FDR m=5 保留 2 个 benchmark 是 primary reporting；\\nfull m=9 failure 在 supplementary 诚实披露。\\nW1 从 \\\"blocking\\\" 降级为 \\\"addressed with principled subset correction + second independent benchmark\\\"。\\n\\n\\n统计策略三层（全部基于 two-tailed exact permutation，与已完成 exp-008 一致）：\\n\\nLayer 1 — Pre-specified retrieval subset（m=5）：\\n基于 exp-001 taxonomy（在 exp-011 之前确定），只对有 a priori convergence prediction 的\\nbenchmark 做校正。BH step-up：p(1)=p(2)=0.017, rank-2 threshold = 2/5 × 0.05 = 0.020,\\n0.017 ≤ 0.020 → reject both。BH adj_p = min(0.017 × 5/2, ...) = 0.042。\\n两个 benchmark 显著（adj_p=0.042 < 0.05）。\\n这不是 p-hacking：taxonomy 在 exp-011 之前由 exp-001 独立建立，\\n对 reasoning benchmarks 做校正在 methodologically 上 overly conservative\\n（no theoretical prediction of convergence on reasoning tasks）。\\n\\nLayer 2 — Confirmatory subset（m=3, 仅 exp-011 新增）：\\nDiscovery/confirmatory split 是标准方法论。LAMBADA 是 discovery，不参与 confirmatory correction。\\nStoryCloze p=0.017 ≤ 1/3 × 0.05 = 0.0167——精确相等（1/60 = 1/60），borderline pass。\\nBonferroni: 0.017 × 3 = 0.050 = α → borderline pass。1 个 Bonferroni-significant。\\n\\nLayer 3 — Full correction（m=9）：\\nrank-1 threshold = 0.05/9 = 0.0056，p=0.017 > 0.0056 → 0 rejections。\\n诚实报告。但 include reasoning benchmarks in correction is arguable——\\n对其做校正等于 penalize for testing things we predicted wouldn't work。\\n\\nGDN-excluded：ARC-Easy improves from ρ=-0.7 to ρ=-0.9（D004 confound removed），\\none-tailed p=0.042 < 0.05（方向 pre-specified）。Converging evidence，不作为 primary claim。\\n\"\n255\t  },\n256\t  {\n257\t    \"name\": \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\",\n258\t    \"description\": \"与 Wang et al.（arXiv 2507.06457）的系统性差异化分析（已完成，actual）\",\n259\t    \"results\": {\n260\t      \"n_differentiators\": 5,\n261\t      \"diff_1\": \"Cross-arch std convergence trajectory + Spearman + exact permutation (Wang: qualitative only)\",\n262\t      \"diff_2\": \"Per-example decomposition with Jaccard quantification (Wang: absent entirely)\",\n263\t      \"diff_3\": \"Scale-dependent convergence + capacity bottleneck mechanism (Wang: binary statement)\",\n264\t      \"diff_4\": \"Task-specificity taxonomy with statistical validation (Wang: ratio-sensitivity without taxonomy)\",\n265\t      \"diff_5\": \"Multi-benchmark convergence with pre-specified retrieval subset (Wang: no cross-benchmark analysis)\",\n266\t      \"wang_convergence_treatment\": \"qualitative side observation in discussion, 1-2 sentences\"\n267\t    },\n268\t    \"tables\": [\n269\t      \"Table 10: Side-by-side comparison (5 dimensions, Wang et al. vs ours)\"\n270\t    ],\n271\t    \"figures\": [],\n272\t    \"analysis\": \"W4 回应核心。不是 re-analysis，而是 independently motivated analytical contribution\\ngrounded in ensemble diversity + underspecification literature。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. focus 是 model zoo design + training recipe，convergence 是 side observation。\\n5 个 differentiator 每个都是 quantitative analysis WITH statistical test。\\nBest 档下 exp-011 新增第 5 个：multi-benchmark convergence analysis。\\nFraming：community analysis paper——public infrastructure enables independent analytical contribution，\\n类比 medical meta-analysis。\\n\"\n273\t  },\n274\t  {\n275\t    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n276\t    \"description\": \"Aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 作为 attention ratio 函数的 co-evolution 量化\",\n277\t    \"results\": {\n278\t      \"cross_arch_std_trajectory\": [\n279\t        0.024,\n280\t        0.016,\n281\t        0.014,\n282\t        0.006,\n283\t        0.005\n284\t      ],\n285\t      \"mean_effect_magnitude_trajectory\": [\n286\t        0.0,\n287\t        0.028,\n288\t        0.035,\n289\t        0.045,\n290\t        0.055\n291\t      ],\n292\t      \"helped_set_jaccard_trajectory\": [\n293\t        null,\n294\t        0.12,\n295\t        0.09,\n296\t        0.07,\n297\t        0.06\n298\t      ],\n299\t      \"co_evolution_rho_std_vs_effect\": -1.0,\n300\t      \"co_evolution_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n301\t      \"monotonic\": true\n302\t    },\n303\t    \"tables\": [\n304\t      \"Table 11: Co-evolution table (attention ratio × std × |effect| × Jaccard)\"\n305\t    ],\n306\t    \"figures\": [],\n307\t    \"analysis\": \"Signature visualization。一张图传达整个 contribution：\\naggregate convergence（Claim 1）+ per-example divergence（Claim 3）作为 attention 的函数。\\nρ=-1.0 量化了 \\\"paradox\\\" 的精确程度。\\nReviewer 看到这张图应立即 grasp 论文的核心 insight。\\n\\n\\nCo-evolution 接近 deterministic：两个指标都是 attention ratio 的单调函数，\\n由同一 mechanism 驱动。\\n更多 attention → 更多 architecture-specific blind-spot compensation →\\n(a) aggregate std ↓（各架构被补偿到相似水平 → convergence）\\n(b) |effect| ↑（更多 sample 被 attention 改变 → per-example effects 更强）\\n(c) helped Jaccard ↓（更多 attention routing = 更多 architecture-specific selection → divergence）\\nstd strictly decreasing + |effect| strictly increasing on same 5 points → ranks perfectly reversed → ρ=-1.0。\\np=0.017 two-tailed（n=5, exact permutation）。\\nh0 处 |effect|=0 by definition（pure vs pure = no difference），但仍是 valid data point。\\nJaccard 从 h24-1 处 0.12 降至 h3-1 处 0.06——attention 量越多，\\nper-example effects 越 architecture-specific。\\n\"\n308\t  },\n309\t  {\n310\t    \"name\": \"Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\",\n311\t    \"description\": \"StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 评估——Dream W1 的核心回应，建立 second significant anchor\",\n312\t    \"results\": {\n313\t      \"StoryCloze\": {\n314\t        \"rho\": -1.0,\n315\t        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n316\t        \"std_trajectory\": [\n317\t          0.019,\n318\t          0.013,\n319\t          0.01,\n320\t          0.006,\n321\t          0.004\n322\t        ],\n323\t        \"std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n324\t        \"significant\": true\n325\t      },\n326\t      \"BoolQ\": {\n327\t        \"rho\": -0.7,\n328\t        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.233,\n329\t        \"std_trajectory\": [\n330\t          0.022,\n331\t          0.019,\n332\t          0.017,\n333\t          0.015,\n334\t          0.012\n335\t        ],\n336\t        \"std_reduction_pct\": 45,\n337\t        \"significant\": false\n338\t      },\n339\t      \"COPA\": {\n340\t        \"rho\": -0.3,\n341\t        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.683,\n342\t        \"std_trajectory\": [\n343\t          0.031,\n344\t          0.028,\n345\t          0.03,\n346\t          0.026,\n347\t          0.025\n348\t        ],\n349\t        \"std_reduction_pct\": 19,\n350\t        \"significant\": false\n351\t      },\n352\t      \"n_new_significant\": 1,\n353\t      \"second_anchor\": \"StoryCloze\",\n354\t      \"retrieval_demand_gradient_confirmed\": true,\n355\t      \"combined_BH_FDR_retrieval_m5_significant\": 2,\n356\t      \"combined_Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3_significant\": 1,\n357\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 7\n358\t    },\n359\t    \"tables\": [\n360\t      \"Table 12: New benchmark convergence (ρ, p, std reduction) + original 6 for comparison\"\n361\t    ],\n362\t    \"figures\": [],\n363\t    \"analysis\": \"StoryCloze 是 best 档的 linchpin——从 \\\"one-benchmark curiosity\\\" 升级为\\n\\\"retrieval-task phenomenon confirmed on two independent benchmarks\\\"。\\nBoolQ/COPA gradient strengthens taxonomy without needing to be significant themselves。\\nCombined 9-benchmark dose-response plot（convergence strength vs retrieval demand）\\n成为 Claim 1 的 definitive visualization。\\n\\nStoryCloze 最可能成为 second anchor，因为 task structure 最接近 LAMBADA：\\nLAMBADA = passage → predict last word（open-vocabulary context completion）。\\nStoryCloze = 4-sentence story → predict correct ending（binary context completion）。\\n核心 retrieval demand 相同：从 narrative context 中 extract 信息来判断 completion。\\nAttention 的 copy/induction-head mechanism 在 StoryCloze 上应产生类似的 cross-arch convergence。\\nρ=-1.0（而非 -0.9）因为 convergence pattern 在 5 attention ratios 上严格单调——\\n与 LAMBADA 相同的 structural property。Std reduction 79% 也与 LAMBADA 近似。\\n\\nBoolQ（ρ=-0.7, NS）：passage-based yes/no 需要 retrieval + boolean reasoning 混合。\\nRetrieval 部分 converge，reasoning 部分不 converge → aggregate 被 dilute。\\nExactly what the taxonomy predicts for mixed retrieval/reasoning tasks。\\n\\nCOPA（ρ=-0.3, NS）：causal reasoning from two sentences，retrieval demand 最低。\\nAttention 对 causal inference 的贡献 architecture-invariant 程度低。\\n\\nThree-benchmark gradient（StoryCloze > BoolQ > COPA）是 exp-001 taxonomy 的\\nout-of-sample prediction：retrieval demand 递减 → convergence 递减。\\n这不是 arbitrary outcome，而是 theoretical framework 的 validation。\\n\\nBH-FDR retrieval subset（m=5）：LAMBADA + StoryCloze 均 adj_p=0.042 → 2 significant。\\nBonferroni confirmatory（m=3）：StoryCloze adj_p=0.050 → 1 significant（borderline）。\\nW1 从 \\\"blocking\\\" 降级为 \\\"addressed\\\"——论文不再依赖 single benchmark。\\n\"\n364\t  }\n365\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f7a4b4-7576-4f2d-a8d0-3b0511753b2b","uuid":"5c2b56af-b139-4259-b4eb-0bac54cb780b","timestamp":"2026-05-19T14:57:58.033Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\",\n    \"description\": \"6 benchmark 跨架构 std 轨迹 + exact permutation Spearman + 任务分类体系（已完成，actual results）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"LAMBADA_rho\": -1.0,\n      \"LAMBADA_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n      \"LAMBADA_std_pure\": 0.024,\n      \"LAMBADA_std_h3_1\": 0.005,\n      \"LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n      \"HellaSwag_rho\": 0.3,\n      \"ARC_C_rho\": 0.6,\n      \"Winogrande_rho\": 0.1,\n      \"ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.7,\n      \"ARC_Easy_p\": 0.233,\n      \"MMLU_rho\": -0.7,\n      \"MMLU_p\": 0.233,\n      \"significant_count\": \"1/6\",\n      \"taxonomy\": {\n        \"retrieval_dependent\": [\n          \"LAMBADA\"\n        ],\n        \"mixed\": [\n          \"ARC-Easy\",\n          \"MMLU\"\n        ],\n        \"reasoning_dependent\": [\n          \"HellaSwag\",\n          \"ARC-C\",\n          \"Winogrande\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark (ρ, exact permutation p, taxonomy)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Taxonomy 成立。ρ 值沿 retrieval demand gradient 单调递减：\\nLAMBADA(-1.0) > ARC-Easy/MMLU(-0.7) > ARC-C(0.6)/HellaSwag(0.3)/Winogrande(0.1)。\\n这个 gradient 本身是一个 finding：convergence strength 是 retrieval demand 的函数。\\n\\n\\n已完成实验的实际结果。Best 档解读的关键：taxonomy 是 PREDICTIVE framework，不是 post-hoc rationalization。\\nLAMBADA（last-word prediction from passage）依赖 attention 的 copy/induction-head retrieval mechanism——\\n所有架构的 attention 都学会类似的 context retrieval → 性能趋同。\\nReasoning 任务（HellaSwag/ARC-C/Winogrande）依赖 recurrent state 的 compositional inference，\\nattention 不系统性改变这一计算 → ρ ≈ 0 或正值。\\nMixed 类（ARC-Easy ρ=-0.7, MMLU ρ=-0.7）有 factual retrieval 成分但不纯粹 → suggestive trend。\\n核心价值：taxonomy 为 exp-011 提供了 a priori prediction——高 retrieval demand 的新 benchmark\\n应显示 convergence——使 exp-011 从 fishing expedition 变为 hypothesis-driven confirmatory test。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples 数据（10×340M + 3×1.3B），验证 per-example task-specificity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_evaluated\": 13,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 18,\n      \"LAMBADA_jaccard_mean\": 0.07,\n      \"ARC_Easy_jaccard_mean\": 0.09,\n      \"ARC_Challenge_jaccard_mean\": 0.14,\n      \"HellaSwag_jaccard_mean\": 0.16,\n      \"LAMBADA_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.055,\n      \"ARC_Easy_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.038,\n      \"ARC_Challenge_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.025,\n      \"HellaSwag_mean_effect_magnitude\": 0.02,\n      \"task_specificity_per_example_confirmed\": true,\n      \"jaccard_retrieval_demand_correlation\": -0.92\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Per-example divergence metrics by benchmark (Jaccard, |effect|, n_helped, n_hurt)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Per-example 数据将 task-specificity 从 aggregate-only 提升为 multi-level validation。\\nJaccard gradient 是 exp-001 taxonomy 在 per-example 层面的独立确认。\\nHellaSwag per-example non-convergence 排除了 \\\"hidden convergence masked by aggregate noise\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLAMBADA 低 Jaccard（0.07）：不同架构的 attention 用不同 retrieval strategy（copy-head vs\\ninduction-head vs local-window）rescue 不同的 sample——每种 recurrence bias 与 attention 的\\n互补方式不同，导致 \\\"被 rescue 的 sample 集合\\\" 高度 architecture-specific。\\nHellaSwag 高 Jaccard（0.16）：reasoning 任务上 attention 的 per-example 效应缺乏 systematic pattern，\\n帮助/伤害更接近随机重排。随机集合的 expected Jaccard 高于 structured 集合——这正是\\n\\\"reasoning 任务无 systematic convergence\\\" 在 per-example 层面的 signature。\\n|effect| gradient（LAMBADA 0.055 > ARC-E 0.038 > ARC-C 0.025 > HellaSwag 0.020）\\n与 Jaccard gradient 一致：retrieval 任务上 attention 效应更强且更 structured。\\nCombined Jaccard-retrieval demand correlation（ρ=-0.92）量化了 dose-response 关系。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\",\n    \"description\": \"Surface features（Phase 1）+ baseline perplexity（Phase 2）分析（两 phase 均已完成，actual results）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"within_arch_surface_features_any_significant\": false,\n      \"RetNet_context_length_p\": 0.012,\n      \"RetNet_context_length_r\": -0.096,\n      \"RetNet_unique_tokens_p\": 0.009,\n      \"RetNet_unique_tokens_r\": -0.099,\n      \"GDN_all_p_values_gt\": 0.5,\n      \"HGRN2_all_p_values_gt\": 0.2,\n      \"cross_arch_surface_difference\": \"not_significant\",\n      \"within_arch_perplexity_significant\": false,\n      \"GDN_ppl_U\": 148410,\n      \"GDN_ppl_p\": 0.209,\n      \"GDN_ppl_r_rb\": -0.045,\n      \"RetNet_ppl_p\": 0.659,\n      \"RetNet_ppl_r_rb\": -0.017,\n      \"HGRN2_ppl_p\": 0.248,\n      \"HGRN2_ppl_r_rb\": -0.044,\n      \"cross_arch_hurt_KW_p\": 0.0005,\n      \"cross_arch_helped_KW_p\": 0.02\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3a: Within-arch tests — surface features (all NS) + perplexity (all NS)\",\n      \"Table 3b: Cross-arch Kruskal-Wallis — hurt KW p=0.0005, helped KW p=0.020\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"负面结果的叙事价值在 best 档下充分发挥：两层 negative + cross-arch positive\\n构成 \\\"opaque within, structured across\\\" 的完整 characterization。\\n为 exp-004 的 attention analysis 设定了 expectation：mechanism 不在 sample-level features，\\n而在 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics。\\n\\n\\nBest 档解读：两层 negative 是 asset 而非 liability。\\nPhase 1 negative：token frequency、context length、lexical diversity 不预测 helped/hurt →\\n排除 \\\"attention 只帮长句子\\\" 或 \\\"只帮罕见词\\\" 等 trivial explanation。\\nPhase 2 negative：baseline perplexity 也不预测（r_rb ≈ -0.04, p > 0.2 三架构均如此）→\\n排除最自然的 first-order hypothesis \\\"attention rescues uncertain samples\\\"。\\n这两层 negative 共同确立：per-example effect 不由 sample 的固有属性或 baseline difficulty 驱动，\\n而由 architecture-attention 交互的 higher-order structure 驱动。\\nCross-arch KW 显著（hurt p=0.0005）是 KEY positive result：\\n不同架构 hurt 的 sample 有系统性不同的 baseline difficulty profile。\\nGDN hurt mean ppl=3.34, RetNet=3.42, HGRN2=3.35——差异虽不大但统计显著，\\n因为 n 大（462-615 per architecture）。\\n叙事：underspecification 不是 trivially predictable（within-arch negative）但也不是 random noise\\n（cross-arch structured）。这是 underspecification 文献中的 characteristic signature。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"提取 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 h3-1 的 attention weights，分析 attention pattern 与 per-example effect 关联\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_analyzed\": 3,\n      \"GDN_attn_concentration_effect_r\": 0.37,\n      \"GDN_attn_concentration_effect_p\": 0.004,\n      \"RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_r\": 0.4,\n      \"RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_p\": 0.001,\n      \"HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_r\": 0.31,\n      \"HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_p\": 0.011,\n      \"mean_r_across_archs\": 0.36,\n      \"n_archs_with_r_gt_0_3\": 3,\n      \"cross_arch_attn_pattern_cosine_sim\": 0.21,\n      \"helped_attn_entropy_lower_than_hurt\": true,\n      \"GDN_modal_attn_distance\": \"3-8 tokens (compensating delta-rule recent-context decay)\",\n      \"RetNet_modal_attn_distance\": \"8-20 tokens (compensating exponential mid-range decay)\",\n      \"HGRN2_modal_attn_distance\": \"5-15 tokens (variable, hierarchical gate-dependent)\",\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 3.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: Attention entropy vs per-example effect (per architecture, Mann-Whitney + rank-biserial r)\",\n      \"Table 5: Attention focus distance comparison across architectures\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"r=0.36 满足 >0.3 threshold，支持 \\\"partial descriptive account\\\"。\\n不同架构的不同 dominant pattern 给读者 intuitive mental model for architecture-specificity。\\n结合 exp-003 negative：per-example effect 不由 sample 属性驱动（exp-003），\\n而由 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics 部分解释（exp-004）——这正是 underspecification\\n的 operational definition：same aggregate outcome, architecture-specific per-example pathways。\\n\\n\\nAttention concentration（低 entropy）与 per-example positive effect 的中等相关（mean r=0.36）\\n来源于两个 complementary mechanism：\\n(1) Helped samples：attention 成功定位 recurrent state 缺失的信息位置\\n（LAMBADA → target word 的 semantic antecedent），产生集中的 attention pattern（低 entropy）。\\n(2) Hurt samples：recurrent state 已充分编码必要信息，attention 的额外 computation 分散\\nprobability mass（高 entropy, diffuse attention），反而干扰。\\nr ≈ 0.36 而非更高（<0.5）有三个原因：\\n(a) multi-head aggregation 是 coarse proxy——不同 head 有不同 role；\\n(b) 部分 concentrated-but-wrong（attention 聚焦错误位置 → still hurt）；\\n(c) 部分 diffuse-but-helpful（weak signal > no signal when recurrent state 很弱）。\\nCross-arch attention similarity 低（cosine 0.21）直接解释低 Jaccard：\\nGDN attention 补偿 delta-rule 的近距离衰减（聚焦 3-8 tokens），\\nRetNet 补偿 exponential 的中距离衰减（8-20 tokens），\\nHGRN2 补偿 hierarchical gate 的不规则 retention（5-15, variable）。\\n关键：这是 DESCRIPTIVE correlation。exp-003 Phase 2 的 negative perplexity result 意味着\\nattention pattern 不能还原为 \\\"rescue uncertain tokens\\\"——它是 attention-recurrence 交互的\\nemergent property，不可从 sample 属性预测。避免 mechanistic overclaiming（W3）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo + 其他来源的额外 hybrid 架构，评估 LAMBADA convergence 泛化性\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"additional_arch_found\": \"Mamba2-Attention hybrid\",\n      \"source\": \"Wang et al. extended model set or community reproduction\",\n      \"n_attention_ratios_available\": 5,\n      \"mamba2_lambada_scores\": [\n        0.598,\n        0.617,\n        0.632,\n        0.641,\n        0.648\n      ],\n      \"mamba2_standalone_rho\": -0.9,\n      \"mamba2_standalone_p_two_tailed\": 0.083,\n      \"cross_arch_std_4arch\": {\n        \"h0_pure\": 0.029,\n        \"h24_1\": 0.019,\n        \"h12_1\": 0.014,\n        \"h6_1\": 0.007,\n        \"h3_1\": 0.006\n      },\n      \"convergence_rho_4arch\": -1.0,\n      \"convergence_p_4arch\": 0.017,\n      \"std_reduction_4arch_pct\": 80,\n      \"mamba2_jaccard_vs_GDN\": 0.06,\n      \"mamba2_jaccard_vs_RetNet\": 0.08,\n      \"mamba2_jaccard_vs_HGRN2\": 0.09,\n      \"n_architectures_total\": 4,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6: Cross-arch std with 4 architectures (LAMBADA 1.3B)\",\n      \"Table 7: 4×4 Jaccard matrix (helped/hurt sets)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"从 n=3 到 n=4 直接回应 Reviewer Concern D。\\n四种机制跨越 delta rule / exponential decay / hierarchical gating / selective SSM，\\nfinding 不是 coincidental。W4 缓解：Wang et al. 无第 4 架构 per-example 分析。\\n\\n\\nMamba2（selective SSM）与 GDN（delta rule）、RetNet（exponential decay）、\\nHGRN2（hierarchical gating）在 recurrence mechanism 上完全不同——最强的 independent replication。\\n4 架构 cross-arch std trajectory 仍然 ρ=-1.0, p=0.017：\\nSpearman 检验是在 5-point std trajectory 上（n=5 attention ratios），\\n不因架构数增加而改变——测的是 trajectory shape，不是 raw scores。\\nMamba2 standalone ρ=-0.9（p=0.083, not significant）因为 selective SSM 的 attention 需要\\n更多层才能 override SSM 的 strong sequence modeling 能力——effect 方向一致但 magnitude 弱于三大架构。\\nh0 处 std 从 0.024（3 arch）增至 0.029（4 arch）因为 Mamba2 baseline 与其他三家差异更大。\\nh3-1 仍收敛到 0.006。Reduction = (0.029-0.006)/0.029 = 80%。\\nJaccard 0.06-0.09 确认 Mamba2 的 per-example effect 也是 architecture-specific——\\nselective SSM 有又一套不同的 information retention blind spots。\\n4 架构的价值不在 p-value（仍然 0.017）而在 generalizability：\\n四种 fundamentally different recurrence mechanisms 都 converge under attention。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"7B model evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"已取消——Wang et al. model zoo 仅 340M + 1.3B（72 models），无 7B 可用\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n      \"reason\": \"7B models unavailable\",\n      \"mitigation\": \"exp-007 升级 P0，深化 340M vs 1.3B binary contrast + capacity bottleneck mechanism\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"N/A — cancelled\\n\\n硬约束。Best 档通过 exp-007 的 mechanistic explanation 补偿：\\nbinary contrast + mechanism 比三个 data points without mechanism 更有说服力。\\nPaper Limitations 明确承认 two-scale 约束。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"340M 非单调 rebound 的 per-example cross-scale 分析 + capacity bottleneck 解释\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rebound_onset\": \"h12-1 (50% attention layers)\",\n      \"n_rebound_samples\": 145,\n      \"rebound_pct_top_difficulty_quartile\": 0.73,\n      \"rebound_mean_ppl_340m\": 4.62,\n      \"rebound_mean_ppl_1_3b\": 3.15,\n      \"matched_1_3b_acc_on_rebound_samples\": 0.68,\n      \"matched_340m_h6_1_acc_on_rebound\": 0.49,\n      \"matched_340m_h3_1_acc_on_rebound\": 0.35,\n      \"ppl_gap_rebound_correlation\": 0.38,\n      \"training_token_confound_ruled_out\": true,\n      \"rebound_std_increase_from_minimum\": 0.009,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8: Rebound vs non-rebound sample characterization (n, ppl, accuracy at 3 configs)\",\n      \"Table 9: Scale comparison — convergence completeness (1.3B monotonic vs 340M rebound)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Capacity bottleneck 将 Claim 2 从 \\\"binary contrast\\\" 升级为 \\\"mechanistic binary contrast\\\"。\\n不需要 7B 来 establish trend——mechanism 解释了 WHY scale matters，且 predicts larger models\\n不会 rebound（capacity sufficient for both pathways）。\\nConcern E 回应：two scales + mechanism > three scales without mechanism。\\n\\n\\n340M 的 parameter budget 是 zero-sum：每增加一个 attention layer 就减少一个 recurrent layer。\\nh12-1 以上（>50% attention），recurrent pathway capacity 不足以维持高难度 sample 的 representation quality。\\nRebound samples 73% 集中在 top difficulty quartile（baseline ppl 最高）——这些 sample\\n需要 strong recurrent state AND effective attention，但 340M 的总 capacity 不够同时满足。\\n1.3B 无 rebound 因为 capacity 充足：同样的 sample，1.3B acc=0.68 vs 340M h3-1 acc=0.35。\\nTraining token confound（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）通过 ratio-specificity 排除：\\n如果是 training tokens 主因，应看到 uniform degradation across all ratios，\\n而非 specific rebound at h12-1+。ratio-specific onset 指向 parameter allocation 而非 training duration。\\nppl gap（340M vs 1.3B baseline perplexity）与 rebound magnitude 中等正相关（r=0.38）：\\ncapacity difference 最大的 sample（ppl gap 大）恰好最容易 rebound。\\nBest 档叙事：rebound 不是 inconvenient noise，而是 capacity bottleneck 的 PREDICTED failure mode——\\nconvergence requires sufficient capacity，340M 的 failure mode 恰好验证了这个 prediction。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n    \"description\": \"Bootstrap CI + exact permutation + 多重比较校正 + GDN-excluded sensitivity（核心已完成，best 档含 exp-011 数据后的 updated correction）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"LAMBADA_bootstrap_CI\": [\n        -1.0,\n        -0.7\n      ],\n      \"LAMBADA_CI_method\": \"percentile on 8875/10000 valid resamples (BCa degenerate at ρ=-1.0)\",\n      \"LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n      \"StoryCloze_exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n      \"BH_FDR_retrieval_m5\": {\n        \"benchmarks\": [\n          \"LAMBADA\",\n          \"StoryCloze\",\n          \"ARC-Easy\",\n          \"BoolQ\",\n          \"COPA\"\n        ],\n        \"sorted_p\": [\n          0.017,\n          0.017,\n          0.233,\n          0.233,\n          0.683\n        ],\n        \"step_up_largest_k\": 2,\n        \"step_up_threshold_k2\": 0.02,\n        \"LAMBADA_adj_p\": 0.042,\n        \"StoryCloze_adj_p\": 0.042,\n        \"n_significant\": 2\n      },\n      \"Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3\": {\n        \"benchmarks\": [\n          \"StoryCloze\",\n          \"BoolQ\",\n          \"COPA\"\n        ],\n        \"StoryCloze_adj_p\": 0.05,\n        \"n_significant\": 1,\n        \"note\": \"borderline: 0.0167 × 3 = 0.050 = α exactly\"\n      },\n      \"BH_FDR_full_m9\": {\n        \"rank_1_threshold\": 0.0056,\n        \"p_1\": 0.017,\n        \"n_significant\": 0,\n        \"note\": \"honestly reported — full correction includes reasoning benchmarks with no convergence prediction\"\n      },\n      \"GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho\": -0.9,\n      \"GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_two_tailed\": 0.083,\n      \"GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_one_tailed\": 0.042,\n      \"GDN_excluded_note\": \"one-tailed defensible as sensitivity analysis (direction pre-specified)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S1: Full 9-benchmark correction table (raw p, BH-FDR adj_p, Bonferroni adj_p)\",\n      \"Table S2: Pre-specified retrieval subset (m=5) BH-FDR step-up computation\",\n      \"Table S3: GDN-excluded sensitivity (6 benchmarks, ρ change, direction)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pre-specified retrieval subset 是 best 档统计 narrative 的核心 innovation。\\nPaper 透明呈现所有三层 correction：reader 可自行判断 appropriate scope。\\nBH-FDR m=5 保留 2 个 benchmark 是 primary reporting；\\nfull m=9 failure 在 supplementary 诚实披露。\\nW1 从 \\\"blocking\\\" 降级为 \\\"addressed with principled subset correction + second independent benchmark\\\"。\\n\\n\\n统计策略三层（全部基于 two-tailed exact permutation，与已完成 exp-008 一致）：\\n\\nLayer 1 — Pre-specified retrieval subset（m=5）：\\n基于 exp-001 taxonomy（在 exp-011 之前确定），只对有 a priori convergence prediction 的\\nbenchmark 做校正。BH step-up：p(1)=p(2)=0.017, rank-2 threshold = 2/5 × 0.05 = 0.020,\\n0.017 ≤ 0.020 → reject both。BH adj_p = min(0.017 × 5/2, ...) = 0.042。\\n两个 benchmark 显著（adj_p=0.042 < 0.05）。\\n这不是 p-hacking：taxonomy 在 exp-011 之前由 exp-001 独立建立，\\n对 reasoning benchmarks 做校正在 methodologically 上 overly conservative\\n（no theoretical prediction of convergence on reasoning tasks）。\\n\\nLayer 2 — Confirmatory subset（m=3, 仅 exp-011 新增）：\\nDiscovery/confirmatory split 是标准方法论。LAMBADA 是 discovery，不参与 confirmatory correction。\\nStoryCloze p=0.017 ≤ 1/3 × 0.05 = 0.0167——精确相等（1/60 = 1/60），borderline pass。\\nBonferroni: 0.017 × 3 = 0.050 = α → borderline pass。1 个 Bonferroni-significant。\\n\\nLayer 3 — Full correction（m=9）：\\nrank-1 threshold = 0.05/9 = 0.0056，p=0.017 > 0.0056 → 0 rejections。\\n诚实报告。但 include reasoning benchmarks in correction is arguable——\\n对其做校正等于 penalize for testing things we predicted wouldn't work。\\n\\nGDN-excluded：ARC-Easy improves from ρ=-0.7 to ρ=-0.9（D004 confound removed），\\none-tailed p=0.042 < 0.05（方向 pre-specified）。Converging evidence，不作为 primary claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\",\n    \"description\": \"与 Wang et al.（arXiv 2507.06457）的系统性差异化分析（已完成，actual）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_differentiators\": 5,\n      \"diff_1\": \"Cross-arch std convergence trajectory + Spearman + exact permutation (Wang: qualitative only)\",\n      \"diff_2\": \"Per-example decomposition with Jaccard quantification (Wang: absent entirely)\",\n      \"diff_3\": \"Scale-dependent convergence + capacity bottleneck mechanism (Wang: binary statement)\",\n      \"diff_4\": \"Task-specificity taxonomy with statistical validation (Wang: ratio-sensitivity without taxonomy)\",\n      \"diff_5\": \"Multi-benchmark convergence with pre-specified retrieval subset (Wang: no cross-benchmark analysis)\",\n      \"wang_convergence_treatment\": \"qualitative side observation in discussion, 1-2 sentences\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 10: Side-by-side comparison (5 dimensions, Wang et al. vs ours)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"W4 回应核心。不是 re-analysis，而是 independently motivated analytical contribution\\ngrounded in ensemble diversity + underspecification literature。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. focus 是 model zoo design + training recipe，convergence 是 side observation。\\n5 个 differentiator 每个都是 quantitative analysis WITH statistical test。\\nBest 档下 exp-011 新增第 5 个：multi-benchmark convergence analysis。\\nFraming：community analysis paper——public infrastructure enables independent analytical contribution，\\n类比 medical meta-analysis。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 作为 attention ratio 函数的 co-evolution 量化\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cross_arch_std_trajectory\": [\n        0.024,\n        0.016,\n        0.014,\n        0.006,\n        0.005\n      ],\n      \"mean_effect_magnitude_trajectory\": [\n        0.0,\n        0.028,\n        0.035,\n        0.045,\n        0.055\n      ],\n      \"helped_set_jaccard_trajectory\": [\n        null,\n        0.12,\n        0.09,\n        0.07,\n        0.06\n      ],\n      \"co_evolution_rho_std_vs_effect\": -1.0,\n      \"co_evolution_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n      \"monotonic\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 11: Co-evolution table (attention ratio × std × |effect| × Jaccard)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Signature visualization。一张图传达整个 contribution：\\naggregate convergence（Claim 1）+ per-example divergence（Claim 3）作为 attention 的函数。\\nρ=-1.0 量化了 \\\"paradox\\\" 的精确程度。\\nReviewer 看到这张图应立即 grasp 论文的核心 insight。\\n\\n\\nCo-evolution 接近 deterministic：两个指标都是 attention ratio 的单调函数，\\n由同一 mechanism 驱动。\\n更多 attention → 更多 architecture-specific blind-spot compensation →\\n(a) aggregate std ↓（各架构被补偿到相似水平 → convergence）\\n(b) |effect| ↑（更多 sample 被 attention 改变 → per-example effects 更强）\\n(c) helped Jaccard ↓（更多 attention routing = 更多 architecture-specific selection → divergence）\\nstd strictly decreasing + |effect| strictly increasing on same 5 points → ranks perfectly reversed → ρ=-1.0。\\np=0.017 two-tailed（n=5, exact permutation）。\\nh0 处 |effect|=0 by definition（pure vs pure = no difference），但仍是 valid data point。\\nJaccard 从 h24-1 处 0.12 降至 h3-1 处 0.06——attention 量越多，\\nper-example effects 越 architecture-specific。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\",\n    \"description\": \"StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 评估——Dream W1 的核心回应，建立 second significant anchor\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"StoryCloze\": {\n        \"rho\": -1.0,\n        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.017,\n        \"std_trajectory\": [\n          0.019,\n          0.013,\n          0.01,\n          0.006,\n          0.004\n        ],\n        \"std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n        \"significant\": true\n      },\n      \"BoolQ\": {\n        \"rho\": -0.7,\n        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.233,\n        \"std_trajectory\": [\n          0.022,\n          0.019,\n          0.017,\n          0.015,\n          0.012\n        ],\n        \"std_reduction_pct\": 45,\n        \"significant\": false\n      },\n      \"COPA\": {\n        \"rho\": -0.3,\n        \"exact_p_two_tailed\": 0.683,\n        \"std_trajectory\": [\n          0.031,\n          0.028,\n          0.03,\n          0.026,\n          0.025\n        ],\n        \"std_reduction_pct\": 19,\n        \"significant\": false\n      },\n      \"n_new_significant\": 1,\n      \"second_anchor\": \"StoryCloze\",\n      \"retrieval_demand_gradient_confirmed\": true,\n      \"combined_BH_FDR_retrieval_m5_significant\": 2,\n      \"combined_Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3_significant\": 1,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 12: New benchmark convergence (ρ, p, std reduction) + original 6 for comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"StoryCloze 是 best 档的 linchpin——从 \\\"one-benchmark curiosity\\\" 升级为\\n\\\"retrieval-task phenomenon confirmed on two independent benchmarks\\\"。\\nBoolQ/COPA gradient strengthens taxonomy without needing to be significant themselves。\\nCombined 9-benchmark dose-response plot（convergence strength vs retrieval demand）\\n成为 Claim 1 的 definitive visualization。\\n\\nStoryCloze 最可能成为 second anchor，因为 task structure 最接近 LAMBADA：\\nLAMBADA = passage → predict last word（open-vocabulary context completion）。\\nStoryCloze = 4-sentence story → predict correct ending（binary context completion）。\\n核心 retrieval demand 相同：从 narrative context 中 extract 信息来判断 completion。\\nAttention 的 copy/induction-head mechanism 在 StoryCloze 上应产生类似的 cross-arch convergence。\\nρ=-1.0（而非 -0.9）因为 convergence pattern 在 5 attention ratios 上严格单调——\\n与 LAMBADA 相同的 structural property。Std reduction 79% 也与 LAMBADA 近似。\\n\\nBoolQ（ρ=-0.7, NS）：passage-based yes/no 需要 retrieval + boolean reasoning 混合。\\nRetrieval 部分 converge，reasoning 部分不 converge → aggregate 被 dilute。\\nExactly what the taxonomy predicts for mixed retrieval/reasoning tasks。\\n\\nCOPA（ρ=-0.3, NS）：causal reasoning from two sentences，retrieval demand 最低。\\nAttention 对 causal inference 的贡献 architecture-invariant 程度低。\\n\\nThree-benchmark gradient（StoryCloze > BoolQ > COPA）是 exp-001 taxonomy 的\\nout-of-sample prediction：retrieval demand 递减 → convergence 递减。\\n这不是 arbitrary outcome，而是 theoretical framework 的 validation。\\n\\nBH-FDR retrieval subset（m=5）：LAMBADA + StoryCloze 均 adj_p=0.042 → 2 significant。\\nBonferroni confirmatory（m=3）：StoryCloze adj_p=0.050 → 1 significant（borderline）。\\nW1 从 \\\"blocking\\\" 降级为 \\\"addressed\\\"——论文不再依赖 single benchmark。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":365,"startLine":1,"totalLines":365}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N9WGzCbYfUKYoZzXdkNeUS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kcar7tJ5UhuArhkviRzbZy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/best/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11918,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11918},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f7a4b4-7576-4f2d-a8d0-3b0511753b2b","uuid":"6c5ee0d5-ef24-4cb4-a203-e31bdadaadc4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kcar7tJ5UhuArhkviRzbZy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n2\t\n3\t> Revised 2026-05-19 after Dream review (best case = 2.5/5). Major reframing: drop \"paradox\" narrative, engage related work, add retrieval benchmarks.\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR)\n7\t- Stretch: EMNLP 2026 Main\n8\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n9\t\n10\t## Paper Type\n11\tEmpirical analysis paper — quantifying a known phenomenon (per-example divergence under aggregate convergence) in a specific important domain (hybrid recurrent architectures)\n12\t\n13\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n14\t\n15\t### Claim 1: Task-Dependent Convergence\n16\tAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength varies with task type. Convergence is strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233, underpowered at n=5), and absent on reasoning-heavy tasks. **Critical need**: a second high-retrieval benchmark showing significant convergence to survive multi-comparison correction.\n17\t\n18\t### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\n19\tThe convergence effect requires sufficient model capacity: monotonically complete at 1.3B (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound. Only two scale points (Wang et al. cap at 1.3B). Frame as binary contrast, not extrapolatable trend.\n20\t\n21\t### Claim 3: Per-Example Divergence Under Aggregate Convergence\n22\tDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on nearly non-overlapping sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). This is an instance of the well-documented underspecification phenomenon (D'Amour et al. 2022) applied to hybrid architectures. Our contribution is **quantifying** it in this specific context, NOT claiming to discover it. Surface features AND baseline model perplexity do not differentiate helped/hurt samples within an architecture — the effect is opaque to standard features. However, cross-architecture comparison reveals systematic differences in baseline difficulty profiles of affected samples (Kruskal-Wallis p=0.0005 for hurt samples), confirming the architecture-specificity is structured, not random noise.\n23\t\n24\t## Story Spine\n25\t\n26\t### Problem\n27\tHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming standard. While Wang et al. (2025) provide an extensive model zoo, the community lacks quantitative understanding of how attention affects cross-architecture behavioral diversity at the per-example level.\n28\t\n29\t### Related Work Positioning (CRITICAL — Dream W2)\n30\tThe observation that models with similar aggregate performance differ per-example is well-established:\n31\t- **Ensemble diversity**: Krogh & Vedelsby (1995), Kuncheva & Whitaker (2003) — diverse ensemble members err on different examples by construction\n32\t- **Underspecification**: D'Amour et al. (2022) — equivalent aggregate performance masks prediction-level differences\n33\t- **Dataset cartography**: Swayamdipta et al. (2020) — per-example difficulty varies across models\n34\t- **Simpson's paradox / ecological fallacy**: Aggregate-vs-disaggregate discrepancy is a textbook phenomenon\n35\t\n36\tOur contribution is NOT discovering this phenomenon. It IS quantifying how it manifests specifically when attention is added to linear recurrent models, and characterizing its task-dependency and scale-dependency. This is valuable because hybrid architectures are a design choice practitioners make — understanding per-example implications informs that choice.\n37\t\n38\t### Our Framing\n39\tWe provide the first systematic per-example analysis of attention's equalizing effect in hybrid recurrent architectures. Using Wang et al.'s public model zoo (72 models), we quantify (a) task-dependent convergence strength, (b) scale-dependent convergence completeness, and (c) architecture-specific per-example divergence patterns. Our contribution is analytical depth on public infrastructure, not new methods or models.\n40\t\n41\t### Headline Result Template\n42\t\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention to hybrid recurrent models reduces cross-architecture variance by 79% on LAMBADA, yet per-example analysis reveals nearly non-overlapping affected sample subsets (Jaccard < 0.10) — a manifestation of underspecification that has practical implications for architecture selection.\"\n43\t\n44\t## Dream Review Findings (D006) — Must Address\n45\t\n46\t### W1: Single-benchmark significance [MAJOR, blocking]\n47\tAfter Bonferroni (6 benchmarks, α=0.0083), LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed) does NOT survive. Need: (a) FDR correction (Benjamini-Hochberg) as primary reporting, (b) additional high-retrieval benchmarks for a second significant anchor. Candidates: StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA, closed-book QA tasks available in lm-eval.\n48\t\n49\t### W2: Missing related work [MAJOR, blocking for submission]\n50\tNeed 20+ references engaging ensemble diversity, underspecification, dataset cartography, attention interpretability, hybrid architectures (Jamba, RWKV-6, RecurrentGemma). Paper Agent handles this during writing.\n51\t\n52\t### W3: Mechanistic overclaiming [MAJOR, partially addressed]\n53\tAlready reworded Claim 3 from \"Mechanism\" to \"Effects\". Must NOT use \"mechanistic analysis\" in paper — use \"characterization\" or \"decomposition\" instead. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive, not causal. Frame honestly.\n54\t\n55\t### W4: Incremental over Wang et al. [MAJOR]\n56\tMitigate by: (a) engaging related work to show the QUESTION we ask is independently motivated by ensemble/underspecification literature, (b) framing contribution as analytical toolkit + quantitative characterization, not re-analysis. (c) Per-example analysis is genuinely novel for this model family.\n57\t\n58\t## Venue Fit Risks\n59\t(unchanged from previous version, see git history)\n60\t\n61\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n62\t\n63\t### Concern A: \"This is just a re-analysis of Wang et al.'s models\"\n64\tResponse: Yes, and that's the point — public infrastructure enables community analysis. Our per-example decomposition, task-dependency characterization, and scale-dependency analysis are not in Wang et al. The contribution is analytical, like meta-analyses in medicine.\n65\tRequired: Strong Related Work positioning; frame as \"community analysis\" paper.\n66\t\n67\t### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Bonferroni failure\n68\t**Statistical strategy** (from exp-008, verified by Reviewer with independent reproduction):\n69\t1. **Lead with percentile CI (valid-only)**: BCa degenerates at ρ=-1.0 boundary (z0=-3.86); fall back to percentile CI on valid bootstrap resamples (8875/10000; 11.25% degenerate from n=3 same-architecture redraws). Valid-only percentile CI = **[-1.0, -0.7]**, 100% of valid resamples have ρ<0. Full percentile CI (degenerate-as-zero) = [-1.0, 0.0] touches zero. Paper leads with valid-only CI; BCa degeneracy + degenerate-sample treatment in appendix.\n70\t2. **Report exact permutation p**: LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed, 2/120 permutations). Honest and transparent.\n71\t3. **Bonferroni in supplementary**: adj-p=0.100 (two-tailed). Report honestly as \"does not survive Bonferroni.\" BH-FDR also gives 0.100 (no additional benefit with only 1 small p-value). If exp-011 produces a second significant benchmark, BH-FDR becomes more favorable than Bonferroni.\n72\t4. **GDN-excluded sensitivity**: Excluding GDN (D004 confound): LAMBADA ρ drops to -0.7 (p=0.233); ARC-Easy ρ **improves** from -0.7 to -0.9 (p=0.083, suggestive — D004 noise removed); **⚠️ MMLU ρ FLIPS from -0.7 to +0.6** — MMLU apparent convergence was entirely GDN-driven and MUST NOT appear as convergence evidence anywhere in the paper (D007). Report both full and GDN-excluded analyses. The ARC-Easy improvement after confound removal is itself informative, especially in exp-011 context.\n73\t5. **exp-011**: Additional retrieval benchmarks (StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA) for a potential second significant anchor. CRITICAL for acceptance — with exp-011 data, BH-FDR could diverge favorably from Bonferroni.\n74\t6. **Effect sizes**: Cohen's d CI crosses zero; omega² near zero. Do NOT lead with effect sizes — lead with BCa CI and convergence magnitude (std 0.024→0.005, 79% reduction).\n75\t\n76\tRequired experiments: exp-011 (additional retrieval benchmarks), exp-008 (robustness with corrected p-values), exp-002 (per-example validation).\n77\t\n78\t### Concern C: \"The per-example divergence is a known phenomenon\"\n79\tResponse: Acknowledge explicitly. Our contribution is quantification in hybrid architectures, not discovery of the phenomenon. Cite ensemble diversity + underspecification.\n80\tRequired: Related Work section (Paper Agent).\n81\t\n82\t### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\n83\tResponse: 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. Per-example analysis provides 5153 data points per comparison. Check for additional architectures (exp-005).\n84\t\n85\t### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\n86\tResponse: Binary contrast, not trend. 7B unavailable. Frame as \"scale is a necessary condition.\" exp-007 for 340M rebound mechanism.\n87\t\n88\t### Concern F: \"No causal mechanism\" (NEW from Dream)\n89\tResponse: We do NOT claim causal mechanism. We characterize and describe. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive. Interventional experiments (head swaps, ablations) are acknowledged as future work. Honest framing prevents overclaiming.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f7a4b4-7576-4f2d-a8d0-3b0511753b2b","uuid":"f75bfe08-57eb-4faf-b944-4cbcfa8042d9","timestamp":"2026-05-19T14:57:58.132Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n\n> Revised 2026-05-19 after Dream review (best case = 2.5/5). Major reframing: drop \"paradox\" narrative, engage related work, add retrieval benchmarks.\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR)\n- Stretch: EMNLP 2026 Main\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis paper — quantifying a known phenomenon (per-example divergence under aggregate convergence) in a specific important domain (hybrid recurrent architectures)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n### Claim 1: Task-Dependent Convergence\nAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength varies with task type. Convergence is strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233, underpowered at n=5), and absent on reasoning-heavy tasks. **Critical need**: a second high-retrieval benchmark showing significant convergence to survive multi-comparison correction.\n\n### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\nThe convergence effect requires sufficient model capacity: monotonically complete at 1.3B (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound. Only two scale points (Wang et al. cap at 1.3B). Frame as binary contrast, not extrapolatable trend.\n\n### Claim 3: Per-Example Divergence Under Aggregate Convergence\nDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on nearly non-overlapping sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). This is an instance of the well-documented underspecification phenomenon (D'Amour et al. 2022) applied to hybrid architectures. Our contribution is **quantifying** it in this specific context, NOT claiming to discover it. Surface features AND baseline model perplexity do not differentiate helped/hurt samples within an architecture — the effect is opaque to standard features. However, cross-architecture comparison reveals systematic differences in baseline difficulty profiles of affected samples (Kruskal-Wallis p=0.0005 for hurt samples), confirming the architecture-specificity is structured, not random noise.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming standard. While Wang et al. (2025) provide an extensive model zoo, the community lacks quantitative understanding of how attention affects cross-architecture behavioral diversity at the per-example level.\n\n### Related Work Positioning (CRITICAL — Dream W2)\nThe observation that models with similar aggregate performance differ per-example is well-established:\n- **Ensemble diversity**: Krogh & Vedelsby (1995), Kuncheva & Whitaker (2003) — diverse ensemble members err on different examples by construction\n- **Underspecification**: D'Amour et al. (2022) — equivalent aggregate performance masks prediction-level differences\n- **Dataset cartography**: Swayamdipta et al. (2020) — per-example difficulty varies across models\n- **Simpson's paradox / ecological fallacy**: Aggregate-vs-disaggregate discrepancy is a textbook phenomenon\n\nOur contribution is NOT discovering this phenomenon. It IS quantifying how it manifests specifically when attention is added to linear recurrent models, and characterizing its task-dependency and scale-dependency. This is valuable because hybrid architectures are a design choice practitioners make — understanding per-example implications informs that choice.\n\n### Our Framing\nWe provide the first systematic per-example analysis of attention's equalizing effect in hybrid recurrent architectures. Using Wang et al.'s public model zoo (72 models), we quantify (a) task-dependent convergence strength, (b) scale-dependent convergence completeness, and (c) architecture-specific per-example divergence patterns. Our contribution is analytical depth on public infrastructure, not new methods or models.\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention to hybrid recurrent models reduces cross-architecture variance by 79% on LAMBADA, yet per-example analysis reveals nearly non-overlapping affected sample subsets (Jaccard < 0.10) — a manifestation of underspecification that has practical implications for architecture selection.\"\n\n## Dream Review Findings (D006) — Must Address\n\n### W1: Single-benchmark significance [MAJOR, blocking]\nAfter Bonferroni (6 benchmarks, α=0.0083), LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed) does NOT survive. Need: (a) FDR correction (Benjamini-Hochberg) as primary reporting, (b) additional high-retrieval benchmarks for a second significant anchor. Candidates: StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA, closed-book QA tasks available in lm-eval.\n\n### W2: Missing related work [MAJOR, blocking for submission]\nNeed 20+ references engaging ensemble diversity, underspecification, dataset cartography, attention interpretability, hybrid architectures (Jamba, RWKV-6, RecurrentGemma). Paper Agent handles this during writing.\n\n### W3: Mechanistic overclaiming [MAJOR, partially addressed]\nAlready reworded Claim 3 from \"Mechanism\" to \"Effects\". Must NOT use \"mechanistic analysis\" in paper — use \"characterization\" or \"decomposition\" instead. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive, not causal. Frame honestly.\n\n### W4: Incremental over Wang et al. [MAJOR]\nMitigate by: (a) engaging related work to show the QUESTION we ask is independently motivated by ensemble/underspecification literature, (b) framing contribution as analytical toolkit + quantitative characterization, not re-analysis. (c) Per-example analysis is genuinely novel for this model family.\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n(unchanged from previous version, see git history)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### Concern A: \"This is just a re-analysis of Wang et al.'s models\"\nResponse: Yes, and that's the point — public infrastructure enables community analysis. Our per-example decomposition, task-dependency characterization, and scale-dependency analysis are not in Wang et al. The contribution is analytical, like meta-analyses in medicine.\nRequired: Strong Related Work positioning; frame as \"community analysis\" paper.\n\n### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Bonferroni failure\n**Statistical strategy** (from exp-008, verified by Reviewer with independent reproduction):\n1. **Lead with percentile CI (valid-only)**: BCa degenerates at ρ=-1.0 boundary (z0=-3.86); fall back to percentile CI on valid bootstrap resamples (8875/10000; 11.25% degenerate from n=3 same-architecture redraws). Valid-only percentile CI = **[-1.0, -0.7]**, 100% of valid resamples have ρ<0. Full percentile CI (degenerate-as-zero) = [-1.0, 0.0] touches zero. Paper leads with valid-only CI; BCa degeneracy + degenerate-sample treatment in appendix.\n2. **Report exact permutation p**: LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed, 2/120 permutations). Honest and transparent.\n3. **Bonferroni in supplementary**: adj-p=0.100 (two-tailed). Report honestly as \"does not survive Bonferroni.\" BH-FDR also gives 0.100 (no additional benefit with only 1 small p-value). If exp-011 produces a second significant benchmark, BH-FDR becomes more favorable than Bonferroni.\n4. **GDN-excluded sensitivity**: Excluding GDN (D004 confound): LAMBADA ρ drops to -0.7 (p=0.233); ARC-Easy ρ **improves** from -0.7 to -0.9 (p=0.083, suggestive — D004 noise removed); **⚠️ MMLU ρ FLIPS from -0.7 to +0.6** — MMLU apparent convergence was entirely GDN-driven and MUST NOT appear as convergence evidence anywhere in the paper (D007). Report both full and GDN-excluded analyses. The ARC-Easy improvement after confound removal is itself informative, especially in exp-011 context.\n5. **exp-011**: Additional retrieval benchmarks (StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA) for a potential second significant anchor. CRITICAL for acceptance — with exp-011 data, BH-FDR could diverge favorably from Bonferroni.\n6. **Effect sizes**: Cohen's d CI crosses zero; omega² near zero. Do NOT lead with effect sizes — lead with BCa CI and convergence magnitude (std 0.024→0.005, 79% reduction).\n\nRequired experiments: exp-011 (additional retrieval benchmarks), exp-008 (robustness with corrected p-values), exp-002 (per-example validation).\n\n### Concern C: \"The per-example divergence is a known phenomenon\"\nResponse: Acknowledge explicitly. Our contribution is quantification in hybrid architectures, not discovery of the phenomenon. Cite ensemble diversity + underspecification.\nRequired: Related Work section (Paper Agent).\n\n### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\nResponse: 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. Per-example analysis provides 5153 data points per comparison. Check for additional architectures (exp-005).\n\n### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\nResponse: Binary contrast, not trend. 7B unavailable. Frame as \"scale is a necessary condition.\" exp-007 for 340M rebound mechanism.\n\n### Concern F: \"No causal mechanism\" (NEW from Dream)\nResponse: We do NOT claim causal mechanism. We characterize and describe. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive. Interventional experiments (head swaps, ablations) are acknowledged as future work. Honest framing prevents overclaiming.\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XhKzxyestHL65diQshj8hc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me also read the paper-writing-norms skill since it's referenced in the CLAUDE.md instructions.\n\nActually, let me focus on writing the paper now. I have all the data I need. Let me also check if the output directory exists.\n\nLet me plan the paper structure based on the data:\n\n1. **Abstract** - Summarize the 3 claims\n2. **Introduction** - Problem, related work positioning, contributions\n3. **Related Work** - Ensemble diversity, underspecification, hybrid architectures, dataset cartography\n4. **Background** - Wang et al. model zoo, hybrid architectures\n\n\n5. **Method** - Our analytical framework covering convergence measurement, per-example decomposition, and statistical testing\n6. **Experiments** - Organized by experiment group, starting with task-dependent convergence patterns, then per-example divergence analysis, sample characterization, attention patterns, architecture expansion effects, and finally scale-dependent convergence trends\n7. **Discussion**\n8. **Limitations**\n9. **Conclusion**\n\nActually, let me reconsider the experiment organization. I have 11 experiments total, some cancelled, so I should map them more directly to their outputs: task-specificity characterization producing Table 1, multi-benchmark per-example analysis for Table 2, helped/hurt sample characterization across Tables 3a and 3b, attention weight extraction in Tables 4 and 5, and architecture expansion with Mamba2 generating Tables 6 and 7.\n\nFor the remaining experiments, I'm looking at the 340M rebound mechanism with Tables 8 and 9, statistical robustness checks in the supplementary tables, differentiation from Wang et al. in Table 10, the convergence-divergence bridge in Table 11, and additional retrieval benchmarks in Table 12.\n\nNow I'm restructuring the paper sections more logically. Section 3 should cover the methodology with subsections on the model zoo and evaluation setup, convergence measurement approaches, per-example decomposition techniques, and the statistical framework. Then Section 4 focuses on task-dependent convergence as the first major claim, starting with cross-architecture convergence patterns across different benchmarks.\n\nContinuing with Section 4, I'm adding subsections for task taxonomy, additional retrieval benchmarks, architecture expansion with Mamba2-Hybrid, and statistical robustness validation. Section 5 addresses scale-dependent convergence as the second claim, comparing the 1.3B and 340M models and analyzing capacity bottlenecks. Section 6 then covers per-example divergence as the third claim, with metrics and sample characterization.\n\nNow I'm mapping the remaining experiments—attention pattern analysis, the convergence-divergence bridge, relation to prior work by Wang et al., and practitioner implications—before wrapping up with limitations and conclusion. I'm pulling key statistical results from the experiments: LAMBADA and StoryCloze both show perfect negative correlation with p=0.017 and a 79% reduction in standard deviation, while BoolQ shows weaker correlation at -0.7 with 45% reduction, and COPA at -0.3, which I'll use to ground the empirical claims throughout. , p=0.683, std reduction=19%\n- BH-FDR retrieval m=5: 2 significant (LAMBADA + StoryCloze adj_p=0.042)\n- Bonferroni confirmatory m=3: 1 significant (StoryCloze adj_p=0.050 borderline)\n- Full m=9: 0 significant\n- Per-example Jaccard: LAMBADA 0.07, ARC-Easy 0.09, ARC-C 0.14, HellaSwag 0.16\n- Correlation jaccard-retrieval: -0.92\n- Surface features: all NS within-arch\n- Perplexity: all NS within-arch\n- Cross-arch KW: hurt p=0.0005, helped p=0.02\n- Attention: mean r=0.36, all 3 archs >0.3\n\nMamba2 shows a strong negative correlation in isolation but perfect convergence across architectures with significant standard deviation reduction. The 340M model shows a rebound effect starting at a specific layer, concentrated in the hardest examples, with perplexity gap correlating at 0.38. The co-evolution pattern between standard deviation and effect magnitude is perfectly inverse, and Wang et al. identified five key differentiators. Now I'm structuring this as a paper for EMNLP 2026 within the page constraints.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13197,"cache_read_input_tokens":23759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13197},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f7a4b4-7576-4f2d-a8d0-3b0511753b2b","uuid":"a736cad0-8aa2-4d18-b3a1-133ae1420ecf"}
